# Services: external APIs & debrid

Third-party HTTP providers (debrid, metadata APIs, scrapers with API keys, etc.) belong in **service classes**, not ad-hoc client modules.

## Where

- File: `src/lib/server/<name>.service.ts` (e.g. `torbox.service.ts`, `tmdb.service.ts`)
- Class: `export class FooService extends Service`
- Register on [`src/lib/server/services.ts`](src/lib/server/services.ts): `foo() { return new FooService(); }`
- Call sites (remotes, `+page.server`, hooks): `locals.services.foo()` via `getRequestEvent()` / `locals`

## Patterns

- Follow [`services-neverthrow`](services-neverthrow.mdc): methods return `Result` / `ResultAsync`, typed `AppError` with stable `ERROR_CODE`s
- Prefer an **official SDK** when one exists (e.g. `@torbox/torbox-api`); wrap it in the service — do not re-export the SDK from remotes
- Config via `$app/env/private` + `requireConfig` / `isConfigured()` when optional
- Soft fallbacks (e.g. debrid miss → WebTorrent) belong in the **caller** or an explicit service method that documents soft-fail — never throw untyped errors across the remote boundary

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const torbox = locals.services.torbox();
if (torbox.isConfigured()) {
	const cached = await torbox.checkCached(hashes).unwrapOr(new Map());
	const resolved = await torbox.resolveCachedDownload(magnet, hash);
	if (resolved.isOk()) { /* use resolved.value */ }
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — parallel client folder / free functions
import { checkCached } from '#lib/server/torbox/client.js';
// ❌ BAD — raw SDK in a remote
import { TorboxApi } from '@torbox/torbox-api';
```

## Do not

- Add `src/lib/server/<vendor>/client.ts` (or similar) for a new provider
- Call external APIs directly from `*.remote.ts` / `+page.server.ts` when a service should own them
- Hand-roll fetch wrappers when an official SDK covers the endpoints we need
- Skip registering the service on `Services`
